Most of the Wizard's I've tried have been Elves, but I'd be interested
to hear what peoples opinions are on the trade-offs for the Wizard's
race.  I've only just begone to scratch the surface on this.

Elves: I'm not sure about the big picture for these guys (I know they
get inffravision to start, sleep resistance at 4th lvl and a higher
starting int).  I've found it tough to play the protection raquette
early on with them.  The mines in general seem tough until your at a
higher level.

Humans: I had too hard a time without infravision, but this is more a
skill and patience defecit on my part.  I read someone here saying that
they can do better with daggers since they can get a higher strength.

Gnomes: This is what I'm trying now and I'm having a bit of an easier
time with the protection thing.  I can start off in the mines and let
my pet do it's thing.  Starting int is maxed at 19 instead of 20 for
the elves, but that doesn't make much of a difference.  Sleep
resistance is so hard to get.

A lucky (so far) game's afoot :)
